 ["THE MAP makes the Master Header whole on its own as the handbook for writing Smile by hand, with the lens report at a chosen depth as an option. It ships with every prompt output where a version says so, and the trial under Test found a prompt without it kept everything, so shipping it is a choice a version makes."
 "I asked for its name on 20 July 2026. “I'm planning to write a short introduction that tells the model what they are experiencing that also informs them of the Smile Prompt Language, which is put at the top of every instruction. What is the name for that?”, and of the names offered, “I like orientation and invocation”.[[m:2026-07-20]] On 31 July I set what it must do, “As a part of Smile I want one master header that you can use for any model so that it is able to write Smile according to the specification from that header.”, and what it leaves out, “The settings/dial system isn't needed for reading or writing Smile.”[[m:2026-07-31]]"
 "In August it was placed. On 4 August, “put the master header in the default Smile modules section”.[[m:2026-08-04]]"
 "So the Master Header moved from a short introduction without a name in July 2026 to the handbook THE MAP describes for any model to read to write Smile, generated from the version in force and still to be built, across {{moments}} moments and {{quotes}} quotes from {{first}} to {{last}}. The older wish for a prompt that explains itself is followed in [[t:meta-instruction-the-prompt-that-explains-itself]], and the version it is generated from in [[t:version]]."],
